John McCarthy (1956) - first talked about AI during a conference that he organized
Alan Turing Mathison - Used AI to build Bombe Machines that deciphered Nazi coded messages from the Enigma machine during world war ii
	* AI finds it difficult to solve problems that are intuitive to humans: 
		- telling whether a friend is angry or not
		- differentiating between items
		- taking notes
Symbolic AI - AI systems with hard coded rules used to solve well-defined tasks and complex problems
	- Couldn't do
		- image recognition, object detection, object segmentation, language translation, natural language processing tasks 
			ML and DL were designed to solve these tasks
			
AI --> ML --> DL
	AI: entirety
	ML: learn data and answers to formulate rules for complex tasks
	DL: good at working with high dimensional data (where feature engineering using ml approaches seems impossible)

DEEP LEARNING
	Traditional ML: handwritten feature extraction to train algorithms
	DL: modern techniques for automatic feature extraction
	
- In deep learning, each layer performs a certain task
	For a face recognition task
		- The first layer detects edges
		- the second layer detects shapes like nose and ears
		- The final layer detects face or complex objects

Deep learning and Neural Networks are used interchangeably
Neural Networks were inspired by the working of the human brain

DATA is the most important ingredient in the success of deep learning
	- MNIST, COCO, CIFAR, Kaggle etc

The advent of open source Deep Learning frameworks (e.g Theano, TensorFlow, PyTorch, Caffe2 etc) has made it easy to adopt deep learning, else:
	- one would have been an expert in C++ or CUDA to implement DL
		These frameworks has boosted the adoption of deep learning because they abstract away the underlying complications and allow us to focus on the applications
		

PyTorch
This deep learning framework can be used for two different things:
	- Replacing Numpy-like operations with GPU-accelerated operations
	- Building deep neural networks




